WEBVTT

00:19.227 --> 00:21.604
With "A human touch" as our tagline,

00:23.523 --> 00:26.901
we've been in the temp business
for 15 years now.

00:26.985 --> 00:29.654
We've come close to bankruptcy
more than once,

00:29.988 --> 00:34.325
but I've used every dirty trick
in the book to get us back on our feet.

00:34.409 --> 00:38.788
And today, I get to taste the fruits
of all that I've achieved.

00:41.041 --> 00:43.585
Delicious. Not a hint of poison.

00:43.668 --> 00:46.171
No problems, Mr. President.

00:46.463 --> 00:49.257
Tamotsu. You, too, Natsumi.

00:49.340 --> 00:54.763
Congratulations on your marriage.
Pump out a bunch of healthy boys for me.

00:55.430 --> 00:56.556
Cheers!

00:56.806 --> 00:58.391
Cheers!

01:05.607 --> 01:06.608
Mr. President!

01:07.400 --> 01:08.943
You useless piece of...

01:09.027 --> 01:09.903
How?

01:09.986 --> 01:11.237
It wasn't poisoned.

01:11.321 --> 01:13.531
I didn't poison him!

01:36.429 --> 01:38.348
So how'd you do it?

01:38.431 --> 01:42.101
How'd you slip poison past
that hotshot poison taster?

01:43.394 --> 01:46.523
I cultivated an immunity in the taster.

01:46.606 --> 01:48.942
You did? How?

01:49.025 --> 01:53.530
I spent three months
adding minute doses to his food

01:53.988 --> 01:56.658
until he could survive a lethal dose.

01:58.118 --> 02:00.912
But wasn't that a huge pain?

02:00.995 --> 02:02.080
Well, yeah.

02:02.330 --> 02:05.500
No one would expect me
to do something so ridiculous.

02:05.583 --> 02:08.711
That's why we're able to stay in business.

02:09.295 --> 02:12.799
By the way, Hikaru, have you given
any thought to you-know-what?

02:12.882 --> 02:13.716
What do you mean?

02:14.384 --> 02:15.802
Marriage.

02:19.180 --> 02:22.559
Akari, do you seriously think
I could get married?

02:22.642 --> 02:24.894
I don't meet any women in my line of work.

02:24.978 --> 02:25.812
But...

02:25.895 --> 02:27.188
I know.

02:27.689 --> 02:31.901
Grandma wants to make one of us
the new head of the Poison Clan.

02:32.318 --> 02:35.113
When I told her I couldn't
because I'm single,

02:35.196 --> 02:38.199
she matched me up with
a total stranger from a branch family,

02:38.283 --> 02:40.451
and nearly forced me to get hitched.

02:41.619 --> 02:43.746
As if I'm that desperate to get married.

02:44.497 --> 02:47.000
So the line of Poison Masters
ends with me.

02:47.083 --> 02:49.210
I'll spend my life single,

02:49.294 --> 02:51.796
and you should spend yours
with your girlfriend.

02:55.300 --> 02:59.012
Well, it's not like I can see girls
going for you, anyway.

02:59.095 --> 02:59.971
Can it.

03:01.639 --> 03:04.350
(Bug Master)

03:05.226 --> 03:07.395
Long time no see, Bug Master.

03:08.563 --> 03:10.231
Glad to see you haven't changed...

03:11.316 --> 03:12.817
Hey, c'mon, Julia.

03:13.651 --> 03:15.194
Yeah.

03:19.240 --> 03:23.786
I hear the Needle Master
has three kids now. All boys.

03:23.870 --> 03:25.371
The food bills are no joke.

03:26.039 --> 03:29.500
'Course, I plan to spend my life single.

03:29.584 --> 03:31.419
Less stress that way. You know?

03:32.128 --> 03:33.755
About that...

03:34.339 --> 03:38.426
I'm thinking of getting married soon.

03:40.178 --> 03:42.347
She's a nice, quiet girl.

03:42.680 --> 03:45.391
And she accepts me for who I really am.

03:45.475 --> 03:46.476
Seriously?

03:46.559 --> 03:49.520
Didn't think I had it in me, did you?

03:49.604 --> 03:53.524
To be honest, I figured you had
even less chance than me.

03:53.608 --> 03:57.362
You wouldn't know it,
but I worked myself to the bone.

03:58.154 --> 04:00.615
Look at you, turning traitor.

04:01.074 --> 04:02.492
Listen, Gero.

04:02.992 --> 04:07.538
Me getting married won't change
the fact we're best buds.

04:07.997 --> 04:09.123
Right?

04:09.374 --> 04:10.208
Right.

04:10.708 --> 04:11.709
Congrats.

04:15.213 --> 04:16.422
See you, Gero.

04:17.674 --> 04:19.592
Let's do this again
when things settle down.

04:20.510 --> 04:22.011
Hey, Bug Master.

04:22.845 --> 04:24.555
You're awesome.

04:25.848 --> 04:31.604
I don't think I could ever find
my special someone like you did.

04:32.855 --> 04:35.525
Marriage never made
a good impression on me,

04:36.150 --> 04:38.528
but seeing you talk about it today,

04:38.611 --> 04:41.781
I found myself thinking
maybe it's not so bad.

04:42.907 --> 04:45.952
Not that it makes
any difference in my case.

04:50.331 --> 04:52.792
It's such an honor to have you here, man.

04:53.209 --> 04:55.712
You seem to be doing
awfully well for yourself.

04:56.379 --> 04:57.672
We owe that to guys like you.

04:58.006 --> 05:01.175
We offer "cleaning" services
at reasonable prices

05:01.259 --> 05:04.429
even your average Joe can afford.

05:05.221 --> 05:09.475
Oh, the ladies work here.
They're assassins-slash-secretaries.

05:09.559 --> 05:13.896
Use them to help with work,
freshen up, or however you like.

05:15.648 --> 05:17.317
No, thank you.

05:17.400 --> 05:20.153
Hmm? That doesn't do it for you?

05:20.236 --> 05:21.654
Ah, wait, Master! That's...

05:22.613 --> 05:26.242
Bulletproof glass partition.
Pretty swanky, huh?

05:27.994 --> 05:31.289
Here's the latest piece of human scum
I'd like your help with.

05:31.372 --> 05:35.668
The heartless marriage swindler,
Mei Kinosaki.

05:35.918 --> 05:39.672
She's been causing all sorts
of trouble on our turf.

05:39.756 --> 05:41.674
Take care of her.

05:44.761 --> 05:48.139
Um, who are you?

05:48.473 --> 05:49.932
You're about to experience...

05:50.516 --> 05:53.478
nerve paralysis in your extremities
that'll work toward your brain.

05:53.561 --> 05:57.607
You'll soon be in agony,
as if you're being ripped to shreds.

05:58.441 --> 06:01.944
And you'll be fully conscious throughout.

06:02.904 --> 06:06.282
Finally, I'll finish you off
with a deadly poison I've concocted.

06:07.241 --> 06:09.535
Time to regret you were ever born.

06:09.619 --> 06:10.453
Um...

06:10.870 --> 06:13.372
My name's Mei Kinosaki.

06:13.456 --> 06:14.290
Have we met be...

06:14.373 --> 06:15.208
Be quiet.

06:16.918 --> 06:18.961
I'm sorry. It's just...

06:20.004 --> 06:23.466
You remind me of my first love.
I had to ask.

06:23.841 --> 06:27.470
So the marriage swindler
is flirting to save her skin?

06:29.305 --> 06:32.683
It's true I conned people.

06:32.767 --> 06:36.270
I needed a lot of money

06:36.354 --> 06:39.357
to save my little brother who's sick.

06:39.649 --> 06:44.070
I took all the loans I could get and
worked jobs I could never admit to anyone,

06:44.153 --> 06:46.614
but it still wasn't enough.

06:50.785 --> 06:56.582
But if I can die with the spitting image
of the man I love watching over me,

06:56.666 --> 06:59.627
maybe life isn't all bad after all.

07:00.628 --> 07:04.132
So please, at least tell me your name.

07:07.468 --> 07:08.386
It's Gero.

07:09.303 --> 07:12.432
Boss, are you sure about this Gero guy?

07:12.515 --> 07:16.352
I mean, he only works targets
who are criminals. "Human scum."

07:16.436 --> 07:18.771
Who does he think he is?

07:18.855 --> 07:20.898
He's a Poison Master.

07:20.982 --> 07:24.902
The Gero family is one of the oldest
in the assassination business.

07:24.986 --> 07:27.280
Anyway, he might have his silly hang-ups,

07:27.363 --> 07:30.158
but he's in high demand.
That makes him the real deal.

07:30.241 --> 07:32.660
Now, let's watch him work.

07:34.328 --> 07:35.455
What?

07:37.540 --> 07:40.835
I'm sorry. Forget I said anything.

07:41.544 --> 07:43.463
Does this woman...

07:44.672 --> 07:45.715
really have...

07:47.967 --> 07:49.510
the hots for me?

07:52.638 --> 07:55.016
Sorry for calling your emergency line.

07:55.349 --> 07:56.184
What's wrong?

07:56.642 --> 07:59.020
I'm moving back to the main house.

07:59.103 --> 08:01.397
I wanted to tell you before I go.

08:01.772 --> 08:02.607
What?

08:03.232 --> 08:06.611
I'll give birth to a new Poison Master.
An heir to the Gero family.

08:07.528 --> 08:09.989
One of the branch family
members is also looking for a partner.

08:10.072 --> 08:12.325
Hey, hang on. You don't need to do that.

08:12.408 --> 08:14.410
You don't get it at all.

08:14.494 --> 08:16.162
Grandma's serious.

08:16.954 --> 08:22.168
She told me so herself. If you don't carry
on the line, and I refuse to...

08:22.251 --> 08:26.255
...they'll take away my freedom
and force me to have babies.

08:26.339 --> 08:29.842
If that's the alternative,
I'd rather go to them on my terms.

08:30.885 --> 08:34.138
Akari, what about your girlfriend?

08:34.222 --> 08:35.932
I'll have to break up with her.

08:36.891 --> 08:37.934
Don't do it.

08:38.309 --> 08:41.521
What do you suggest?
Sacrificing yourself in my place?

08:42.188 --> 08:43.940
That'd be even worse.

08:44.273 --> 08:47.318
When else can I make myself useful?

08:47.985 --> 08:49.403
Wait a minute.

08:51.072 --> 08:53.866
If you don't want to die, marry me.

08:55.618 --> 08:59.372
I need to marry to become
the head of the Poison Clan.

08:59.830 --> 09:03.543
If I have to be with someone,
I want it to be you. At least you like me.

09:03.793 --> 09:06.337
I can help with
your brother's illness, too.

09:09.006 --> 09:14.303
Is it fair for me to be so lucky?

09:17.014 --> 09:18.391
Of course...

09:20.476 --> 09:23.396
there's no way in hell I would.

09:25.398 --> 09:28.317
That's the look I wanted to see.

09:28.401 --> 09:33.864
I mean, I'm gonna die, and it'd piss me
off to go out without getting a shot in.

09:33.948 --> 09:36.325
Man, what a relief.

09:36.409 --> 09:42.498
You see couples and whether it's their
personalities, wealth, looks, or whatever,

09:42.582 --> 09:45.668
they're all together
because they're a good match.

09:45.751 --> 09:49.297
But a piece of shit who proposes
to a target he can just kill anytime

09:49.380 --> 09:51.507
isn't a good match for anyone.

09:52.174 --> 09:53.467
Figures.

09:53.718 --> 09:57.346
Well, at least, if you're serious
about finding someone,

09:57.430 --> 10:00.641
you've got to start by coming clean
about how you really feel.

10:00.725 --> 10:03.769
Everyone finds their ideal partner
by figuring each other out,

10:03.853 --> 10:06.772
butting heads,
and running themselves ragged.

10:07.607 --> 10:12.945
Do you really only want
to get married for an inheritance?

10:16.490 --> 10:17.950
Uh, Master?

10:18.034 --> 10:20.286
Get on with it already.

10:20.369 --> 10:23.664
We're paying good money
to watch you work.

10:24.832 --> 10:29.295
I only dispose of human scum
who deserve to die.

10:30.004 --> 10:32.048
It's not a justice thing.

10:32.381 --> 10:34.925
I just don't take jobs that'd
make it hard to sleep at night.

10:35.176 --> 10:37.720
Of course, murder's still murder.

10:38.262 --> 10:43.601
And yet, I sometimes catch myself wanting
to live in peace with someone I love.

10:44.393 --> 10:46.937
That side of me makes me
sick to my stomach.

10:48.648 --> 10:49.607
The truth is...

10:50.441 --> 10:56.322
I wanna meet someone I like and lead
a fun, happy life as much as the next guy!

10:56.614 --> 11:01.035
One where she asks, "How was your day?"
and we chat before falling asleep,

11:01.118 --> 11:04.997
or she says "What's wrong?" when I cough.

11:05.081 --> 11:06.332
But...

11:07.333 --> 11:10.252
There's no way I'll ever
meet anyone like that.

11:10.336 --> 11:12.922
I never went to school. Not even daycare.

11:13.005 --> 11:16.342
I've lived as a Poison Master
since I was old enough to form memories.

11:16.592 --> 11:19.303
Showing weakness
leads straight to failure.

11:20.262 --> 11:26.352
I could never open up
and bare my heart to a stranger!

11:26.727 --> 11:27.853
So...

11:29.605 --> 11:31.190
What are you talking about?

11:32.233 --> 11:37.196
You just poured your heart out to me,
and we only just met.

11:37.696 --> 11:41.534
You're right that being an assassin
is a big drawback.

11:41.617 --> 11:46.539
But in that case, just work at meeting
all sorts of different people.

11:46.622 --> 11:50.543
If you put yourself out there
and keep at it till you're worn-out,

11:51.043 --> 11:54.797
someone who's into you
is bound to turn up.

11:54.880 --> 11:57.842
'Course, it'll probably be hell.

11:59.135 --> 12:01.595
Now, get it over with.

12:01.679 --> 12:03.722
I'm human scum.

12:03.806 --> 12:08.060
My brother's medical bills won't get paid
because I screwed up.

12:08.561 --> 12:12.148
I'm taking away the future of the person
I care about the most.

12:13.357 --> 12:15.359
How much scummier could I get?

12:16.861 --> 12:18.362
Master Gero.

12:18.446 --> 12:19.947
Why don't ya call it there?

12:20.030 --> 12:23.451
You already got plenty of dating advice
out of that marriage swindler.

12:23.534 --> 12:26.829
Now, finish this scumbag off.

12:27.580 --> 12:28.914
No.

12:29.415 --> 12:31.041
I need you.

12:31.876 --> 12:34.920
Only an expert matchmaker
could marry all those people.

12:35.337 --> 12:37.798
So I want to hire you
in that capacity.

12:37.882 --> 12:41.051
I'll do everything I can to keep you
and your brother alive.

12:42.219 --> 12:44.930
And in exchange,
you'll help me get married!

12:48.851 --> 12:51.937
I've dated more people than I can count,

12:52.897 --> 12:55.441
but I've never gotten
a proposal like that before.

12:55.858 --> 12:56.901
Still...

12:57.234 --> 12:59.904
That's if you make it
out of here, remember?

12:59.987 --> 13:02.740
I'm real disappointed in you, Master Gero.

13:03.407 --> 13:04.825
You see how it is.

13:04.909 --> 13:06.744
We have a deal.

13:07.995 --> 13:14.335
Killing the Poison Masters' heir apparent
will rocket us to the top of the industry.

13:15.127 --> 13:19.673
You people take jobs from regular folk
at rock-bottom rates,

13:20.132 --> 13:23.511
then use what you know to blackmail them
for the rest of their lives.

13:24.303 --> 13:26.680
How many lives have you ruined?

13:27.014 --> 13:30.643
Like I care. What's wrong
with taking suckers for a ride?

13:30.726 --> 13:32.436
You think you're some kind of hero?

13:32.937 --> 13:35.272
Just making sure you meet my condition.

13:36.440 --> 13:37.691
You're all...

13:46.450 --> 13:47.952
human scum.

13:48.577 --> 13:49.787
Shoot him!

13:49.870 --> 13:51.330
Kill his ass!

14:06.637 --> 14:08.889
Hey, where'd he go?

14:08.973 --> 14:10.891
You get to have a front-row seat.

14:14.019 --> 14:16.230
Now, watch this Poison Master work.

14:19.650 --> 14:22.069
Wow. So I guess...

14:22.152 --> 14:24.989
you're not just all talk?

14:25.072 --> 14:28.075
You really are that good?

14:28.158 --> 14:30.619
They're still nobodies,
even when they gang up.

14:30.703 --> 14:34.081
Anyway, I only used
my "300 Torments of Hell."

14:34.707 --> 14:37.793
They'll live, and the trauma
will keep them out of the business.

14:40.546 --> 14:42.882
Hikaru? You know what I said earlier?

14:42.965 --> 14:44.049
I'm leaving now.

14:44.133 --> 14:44.967
Akari.

14:48.262 --> 14:50.347
You don't need to succeed Grandma.

14:50.431 --> 14:52.850
Like I said, you have no idea what I'm...

14:54.768 --> 14:56.020
I get it now.

14:57.605 --> 15:00.900
Meeting someone you can love
and build a life with

15:00.983 --> 15:03.277
is about as close to a miracle
as you can get.

15:04.236 --> 15:06.780
So you ought to live with your girlfriend.

15:07.990 --> 15:09.825
Tell Grandma...

15:10.576 --> 15:13.370
I'm going to get married
and lead the Poison Clan,

15:13.704 --> 15:18.500
but I'm going to find a partner myself.

15:19.501 --> 15:21.754
Seriously?

15:22.004 --> 15:24.673
You always decide everything on your own.

15:26.050 --> 15:28.719
Well, okay. I'll tell her.

15:32.640 --> 15:35.517
What's the holdup? I can't get around yet.

15:35.601 --> 15:37.937
H-How should I carry you?

15:38.020 --> 15:40.773
I've never touched a girl except on jobs.

15:40.856 --> 15:43.359
Where is it okay to touch?

15:44.276 --> 15:46.362
Oh, don't worry about that.

15:46.695 --> 15:48.113
I mean, I'm a guy.

15:48.530 --> 15:50.240
Oh, in that case...

15:51.700 --> 15:52.534
Huh?

15:55.079 --> 15:57.039
(The Poison Master's Search for a Bride)

15:58.791 --> 16:01.835
A bath after a blowup hits different,
don't you think?

16:01.919 --> 16:03.921
Hey, Gero, wanna join me?

16:04.004 --> 16:04.922
No, thanks.

16:05.798 --> 16:07.549
Come on. Where's the harm?

16:07.633 --> 16:08.676
No, thanks!

16:09.468 --> 16:12.179
Ah, I feel fully alive again.

16:12.513 --> 16:13.639
Kinosaki...

16:13.722 --> 16:16.350
"Doesn't look like any man
I've ever seen"?

16:16.433 --> 16:19.186
Wanna see for yourself?

16:21.063 --> 16:23.649
Why do you wear women's clothes?

16:23.732 --> 16:24.566
What?

16:24.650 --> 16:27.069
Because my latest mark was a man.

16:27.152 --> 16:29.446
I wear men's clothes when I con women.

16:29.530 --> 16:32.032
It's more fun when you can go
both ways, you know?

16:32.116 --> 16:35.536
So, Gero, proposing to me was
the best move you could have made.

16:35.619 --> 16:36.453
Pro...

16:36.662 --> 16:40.666
I can teach you how to hook anyone,
man or woman.

16:40.749 --> 16:42.251
Then, hurry up and...

16:42.334 --> 16:43.377
Here. Look at this.

16:44.211 --> 16:46.880
I've registered you
for a matchmaking party.

16:46.964 --> 16:48.215
Fill in your profile.

16:48.298 --> 16:51.844
Huh? Wait, it's after midnight,
so this is today.

16:52.761 --> 16:53.929
"Profession"?

16:54.805 --> 16:57.599
Wait. Writing the truth
is probably a bad idea.

16:58.017 --> 17:00.602
"Self-employed."

17:01.186 --> 17:04.356
There are way more men
than women coming,

17:04.440 --> 17:08.944
so I'll charm all the men
and leave you with fewer rivals.

17:09.153 --> 17:10.362
Remember, Gero.

17:10.446 --> 17:14.867
Grooming and fashion are just ways
to avoid making a bad impression.

17:14.950 --> 17:17.244
Improving them will only
get you as far as "nice guy."

17:17.578 --> 17:22.291
No one's gonna fall for you unless
we find your charm and bring it out.

17:22.374 --> 17:24.376
Try different approaches and see.

17:26.420 --> 17:28.672
Hello. It's nice to meet you.

17:28.756 --> 17:31.884
My research tells me
first impressions are everything.

17:32.217 --> 17:34.970
I've got the perfect pickup line.

17:35.679 --> 17:36.555
I'm Gero.

17:37.431 --> 17:39.224
I make *** million a year.

17:39.308 --> 17:40.851
What were you thinking?!

17:40.934 --> 17:42.311
She recoiled in horror!

17:42.561 --> 17:46.065
But my "charm" is my income, right?!
It's the top feature in men!

17:46.315 --> 17:50.736
Maybe, but blurting it out right away
makes you a jerk bragging about money!

17:50.819 --> 17:54.782
At least look her in the eyes and smile
before you say anything.

18:08.504 --> 18:11.632
Maybe I'll look up how to smile
when I get home.

18:11.924 --> 18:13.759
Gero, we'll try this next.

18:14.635 --> 18:17.971
A dating app will give you a chance
to settle in and really talk with girls.

18:18.055 --> 18:20.641
I got you a date in seconds.

18:20.724 --> 18:23.060
So let's go bring out your charm.

18:25.062 --> 18:26.605
U-Um...

18:26.897 --> 18:30.150
A Poison Master should never eat anything
someone else serves him.

18:30.234 --> 18:32.736
I developed that instinct
to protect myself,

18:33.112 --> 18:37.324
but I doubt anyone here is out to get me.

18:37.407 --> 18:40.244
So it will be fine! Totally fine!

18:40.327 --> 18:41.829
How was that?

18:44.414 --> 18:46.667
O-Okay, we'll try with this girl next.

18:47.918 --> 18:49.044
N-Next is...

18:51.630 --> 18:52.464
Next.

19:03.767 --> 19:07.813
Just today, I met nearly 30 women,

19:07.896 --> 19:10.691
but I didn't exchange contact info
with a single one.

19:10.774 --> 19:13.944
W-Well, you did the best you could.

19:15.529 --> 19:19.908
Still, I know our goal
is to find your charm,

19:19.992 --> 19:23.662
but I figured you'd hit it off
with at least one of them.

19:23.745 --> 19:24.997
Kinosaki.

19:25.330 --> 19:29.001
Maybe I just don't have any charm.

19:29.084 --> 19:31.295
You do. I know you do.

19:31.378 --> 19:34.131
It's just hidden,
so we can't see what it is yet.

19:34.506 --> 19:37.342
I promise there are people out there
who will be into you.

19:37.676 --> 19:44.057
I'm gonna polish you up and bring out
your charm so you can knock 'em dead.

19:44.641 --> 19:47.561
Actually, I did find one thing
we can work with.

19:47.978 --> 19:48.896
What's that?

19:49.605 --> 19:51.440
You like DIY candy kits.

19:51.523 --> 19:52.357
Huh?

19:52.441 --> 19:55.569
People with niche hobbies
can have a great time chatting.

19:55.652 --> 19:58.238
Also, is it me, or is this cleaner
wicked strong?

19:58.655 --> 20:00.741
I mixed it myself. I call it "Joker."

20:01.200 --> 20:05.204
Using deadly poison to fight stubborn
stains is my favorite way to de-stress.

20:05.579 --> 20:09.416
I can make cleaning agents strong enough
to melt iron when I set my mind to it.

20:09.750 --> 20:12.044
Oh, is this another niche hobby?

20:12.586 --> 20:14.922
Maybe just never mention
this one to anyone, 'kay?

20:18.258 --> 20:19.718
Found you.

20:20.802 --> 20:22.804
Well, my place is this way.

20:23.096 --> 20:24.264
See you tomorrow.

20:24.348 --> 20:25.182
Sure.

20:25.974 --> 20:29.102
Wait, Kinosaki! What do you mean,
"tomorrow"? Where?

20:39.529 --> 20:41.990
(Add Friend)

20:44.284 --> 20:48.413
Mei Kinosaki, what did you do
to my big bro?

20:48.497 --> 20:49.331
Huh?

20:49.414 --> 20:50.874
Don't give me that.

20:51.291 --> 20:54.086
He used to brag he'd
make the living fossils

20:54.169 --> 20:56.296
in this lame-ass biz beg for mercy.

20:56.380 --> 21:01.551
Now he's saying he's gonna take over
the family cleaning service.

21:02.386 --> 21:04.930
Maybe he got tired of life
in the big city?

21:11.144 --> 21:12.896
That was a lead pellet.

21:14.356 --> 21:16.024
Now that look gets my blood pumping.

21:16.108 --> 21:18.902
I'm gonna make you tell me
everything that went down.

21:19.319 --> 21:22.698
If you beg for your life like you mean it,
I might give you another...

21:22.781 --> 21:27.202
I'd rather die than team up with trash
who con regular people.

21:29.830 --> 21:31.581
You've got guts.

21:31.665 --> 21:34.126
But people who make a living off
dirty jobs like ours

21:34.209 --> 21:39.381
and still toss around half-assed morals
about who to target

21:39.464 --> 21:41.258
can't survive in this business.

21:41.717 --> 21:46.388
That pretty face of yours is your weapon.
I'll make sure you can never use it again.

21:46.888 --> 21:49.182
My next shot'll be a shotgun blast.

21:50.600 --> 21:52.102
B-Boss!

21:52.728 --> 21:53.603
Up ahead!

21:56.231 --> 21:57.399
Gero?

21:57.482 --> 21:58.400
Who cares?

21:58.483 --> 22:00.360
Turn him into roadkill!

22:31.099 --> 22:32.851
What the...

22:44.196 --> 22:47.532
Y'know, being a cleaner
doesn't sound so bad.

22:52.954 --> 22:54.372
You dropped this.

22:55.207 --> 22:56.291
Thanks.

22:56.875 --> 22:59.252
Thank you, Kinosaki.

22:59.336 --> 23:03.423
I could never meet so many women
in one day on my own.

23:03.507 --> 23:07.385
Just one rejection would have left me
moping for a lifetime.

23:08.678 --> 23:11.348
I know I'm hopeless,
but I'm counting on you.

23:12.015 --> 23:15.185
You know, I didn't get
anyone's contact info today.

23:15.268 --> 23:16.269
Hey, are you listening?

23:16.353 --> 23:19.689
Gero, would you mind giving me yours?

23:20.524 --> 23:23.068
(Friends: 1)

23:23.151 --> 23:25.987
I doubt my friends list
will ever get any longer.

23:26.404 --> 23:27.572
I don't know why,

23:28.156 --> 23:30.784
but you're dazzling me right now.

23:31.910 --> 23:36.331
I've got it. I've found it.
I've found your charm.

23:37.165 --> 23:41.837
This is the story of the elite assassin
known as the Poison Master, Hikaru Gero,

23:41.920 --> 23:44.089
and his search for a bride.

23:47.676 --> 23:48.635
Today, you're going

23:48.718 --> 23:51.096
- Let's go on another date. No business.
- on your first date... rehearsal!

23:51.179 --> 23:53.098
- What will you say to her?
- No way in hell.

23:53.181 --> 23:54.141
Don't you dare.

23:54.224 --> 23:56.601
Next time: "What is 'Charm, ' Anyway?"
